        "deprecated": false,
        "description": "Identifies `gitsync sync` and `gitsync run`, which force-push and prune every configured repo's branches and tags to GitHub so the two sides end up identical, and can eventually delete the GitHub mirror once a repo disappears from the source (subject to gitsync's own delete_grace and delete_limit safeguards). Both subcommands accept --dry-run, which reports what would happen without pushing or deleting anything.",
        "example_command": "gitsync sync",
        "family": null,
        "fixed_reason": null,
