        "deprecated": false,
        "description": "Identifies `gitsync hooks --force` (rewrites existing webhooks on the git server), `gitsync hooks --remove` (deletes them), and `gitsync install` / `gitsync uninstall` (registers or removes the persistent background service). Plain `gitsync hooks` (no flags) only creates missing webhooks and is not covered. `uninstall` ignores every argument and always removes the service and binary on both Linux and Windows, so it has no safe variant, not even --help/-h.",
        "example_command": "gitsync hooks --remove",
        "family": null,
        "fixed_reason": null,
